---
import Card from "astro-theme-university/components/Card.astro";
import CardGrid from "astro-theme-university/components/CardGrid.astro";
import ContentLayout from "astro-theme-university/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import heroImage from "../assets/images/hero-home.jpg";
import { courseMeta } from "../course-config";
import { sessionLabels, siteConfig } from "../site-config";
---

<ContentLayout
  title={`${courseMeta.code}: ${courseMeta.title}`}
  description={courseMeta.description}
  heroImage={heroImage}
  heroImageAlt="A sprawling Factorio base viewed from above, belts and pipes threading between assemblers toward a rocket silo mid-launch at the centre"
  {...siteConfig}
>
  <ul class="course-tags" aria-label="Course tags">
    {courseMeta.tags.map((tag) => <li>{tag}</li>)}
  </ul>

  <h2>What you will do</h2>
  <p>
    You will spend the semester inside one long-running Factorio save,
    building the systems a real production line needs: smelting and power
    that don't stall, belts and balancers that don't starve each other,
    trains that don't deadlock, and a base you can still reason about once it
    stops fitting on one screen. Every week ends with something running, not
    just something explained. You walk out with a base that survives contact
    with its own success — and a written record of the engineering decisions
    that got it there.
  </p>

  <h2>Who it is for</h2>
  <p>
    Anyone who already knows how to place a belt and wants to know why their
    factory keeps jamming anyway. No prior systems-engineering background is
    assumed, but you should arrive comfortable enough in Factorio's basics
    (or willing to get there in week 1) that the studio time goes on
    logistics problems, not on learning which key places an inserter.
  </p>

  <h2>Where to go next</h2>
  <CardGrid columns={2}>
    <Card title={sessionLabels.plural} href="/sessions/">
      <p>The weekly schedule and what happens in each teaching tutorial.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="Assessment" href="/assessments/">
      <p>What is marked, what it is worth, and when it is due.</p>
    </Card>
    <Card title="People" href="/people/">
      <p>Who teaches the course and how to reach them.</p>
    </Card>
  </CardGrid>
</ContentLayout>

<style>
  .course-tags {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    margin-block: 0 2rem;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .course-tags li {
    padding: 0.25rem 0.65rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    color: var(--at-text-secondary);
    background: var(--at-bg-alt);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }
</style>
